-- title:
--   Formal group coordinates on a connected p-divisible tower over 𝔽ₚ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $h$, and let $G_v$ ($v \in \mathbb{N}$) be commutative rings carrying cocommutative Hopf algebra structures over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, each finite as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module, together with surjective coalgebra-and-algebra maps $s_v \colon G_{v+1} \to G_v$ such that $\dim_{\mathbb{Z}/p} G_v = p^{vh}$, the kernel of $s_v$ is the image of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\text{counit})$ of $G_{v+1}$ under the $p^v$-th convolution power of the identity, and every $G_v$ is a local ring. The assertion is that there exist $d$, a $d$-dimensional formal group law $\Phi$ over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ (a $d$-tuple of power series in $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ variables with vanishing constant term, identity linear terms and the associativity identity) which is commutative in the sense that swapping the two groups of variables fixes each component, and $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra maps $\kappa_v \colon (\mathbb{Z}/p)[[X_1,\dots,X_d]] \to G_v$, with all of the following: each $\kappa_v$ is surjective; $\ker \kappa_v$ is generated by the components of the $p^v$-fold iterate $\Phi.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,(p^v)$ (defined by $0$ at stage $0$ and by substituting the previous stage into $\Phi$); $s_v \circ \kappa_{v+1} = \kappa_v$; the counit kills each $\kappa_v(X_i)$; each $\kappa_v(X_i)$ lies in the radical of the ideal generated by $p$ in $G_v$; $\kappa_v$ is given on all $F$ by $(p)$-adic evaluation at the coordinates $\kappa_v(X_i)$; the comultiplication of $\kappa_v(X_i)$ equals the $(p)$-adic evaluation of $\Phi_i$ in $G_v \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p} G_v$ at the two families $\kappa_v(X_j) \otimes 1$ and $1 \otimes \kappa_v(X_j)$; $\dim_{\mathbb{Z}/p} (\mathbb{Z}/p)[[X]]/(\Phi.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,p) = p^h$; $d$ is the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-dimension of the cotangent module $I/I^2$ of the augmentation ideal $I$ of $G_1$; for every $N$ some $\ker \kappa_v$ is contained in $(X_1,\dots,X_d)^N$; the $\kappa_v$ are jointly injective; and every family $(z_v)$ compatible under the $s_v$ is of the form $(\kappa_v(F))_v$ for a single power series $F$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$p$ coordinatisation of a connected $p$-divisible group in the style of Tate's structure theorem: the tower of finite Hopf algebras is identified with a power series ring equipped with a commutative formal group law, with $[p^v]_\Phi$ cutting out the $v$-th level, and the final three clauses express that the $\kappa_v$ realise $\varprojlim G_v \cong (\mathbb{Z}/p)[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$. It is used in the construction of Honda systems, via [`Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_mvFormalGroup_basis_coeff_eq_normalForm`](thm.html#Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_mvFormalGroup_basis_coeff_eq_normalForm).
